# Line endings are part of the experiment, not a cosmetic preference.
#
# The V0 harness reads fixture files with `fs::read_to_string` and packs them
# under a byte budget, so a CRLF checkout fits fewer documents into the same
# budget and produces different context bytes. A fresh clone on a host with
# `core.autocrlf=true` therefore did NOT reproduce the sealed V0 results.
# See bench/V0/ARCHIVE.md erratum E-3.
#
# Pinning LF makes every checkout byte-identical on every platform, which is a
# precondition for an external executor reproducing a sealed benchmark.
#
# (R1 is unaffected by construction -- its .scn parser normalises through
# `str::lines()`. That was verified, not assumed, and is recorded in
# bench/R1/STATUS.md. This file protects it regardless.)

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
